/* Decision — what is known of a proposition, as a value to eliminate.
 *
 * A proposition has three values, and leaving the classifier toward the two
 * values of Boolean would lose one: unknown is not absent. `decide(p)` is
 * total and lands here, in a coproduct of three arms; whoever uses it gives
 * an answer for each arm with `match`, the third one included, because a
 * coproduct is left only by an arrow out of every arm. */
place Decision { this > Present :U Absent :U Unknown }
